                                                       "- `'k-means++'` : selects initial cluster centers for "
                                                       'k-mean\n'
                                                       '  clustering in a smart way to speed up convergence. See '
                                                       'section\n'
                                                       '  Notes in k_init for more details.\n'
                                                       "- `'random'`: choose `n_clusters` observations (rows) at "
                                                       'random from data\n'
                                                       '  for the initial centroids.\n'
                                                       '- If an array is passed, it should be of shape '
                                                       '`(n_clusters, n_features)`\n'
                                                       '  and gives the initial centers.\n'
