                                                        'multivariate\n'
                                                        '  return (2-dim when predicting for several '
                                                        'observations).\n'
                                                        '  The probabilities in the truncated region are zero.\n'
                                                        "- 'prob-base' : probabilities for untruncated base "
                                                        'distribution.\n'
                                                        '  The probabilities are for each count from 0 to '
                                                        'max(endog), or\n'
                                                        '  for y_values if those are provided. This is a '
