                                                                'preserving the values at the corner pixels.\n'
                                                                '        If set to ``False``, the input and '
                                                                'output tensors are aligned by the corner\n'
                                                                '        points of their corner pixels, and the '
                                                                'interpolation uses edge value padding\n'
                                                                '        for out-of-boundary values, making this '
                                                                'operation *independent* of input size\n'
                                                                '        when :attr:`scale_factor` is kept the '
                                                                'same. This only has an effect when '
                                                                ':attr:`mode`\n'
